---Brand settings. See [Brands](#brands)
---@class zendesk.AccountSettingsBrandsObject
---@field brand_user_separation_scope_query_default? zendesk.AccountSettingsBrandsObjectBrandUserSeparationScopeQueryDefault Controls which users the [List Users](/api-reference/ticketing/users/users/#list-users), [Count Users](/api-reference/ticketing/users/users/#count-users), [Search Users](/api-reference/ticketing/users/users/#search-users) and [Autocomplete Users](/api-reference/ticketing/users/users/#autocomplete-users) endpoints return when an external request omits `brand_id`. * `"0"` — customers in non-separated brands and all team members (default). A string, matching the `brand_id=0` (account scope) value of the users endpoints. * `"default_brand"` — customers in the default brand and all team members. Falls back to `"0"` if the default brand doesn't have user separation enabled. * `"all"` — customers and team members across all brands, within the caller's permissions. * `"error"` — reject the request with `400 Bad Request` and `{"error": "brand_id parameter is required"}`. Integrations that don't send `brand_id` stop working. Only returned, and only writable, when brand separation is available on the account. Only admins can update it. Any other stored value is treated as `"0"`.
---@field default_brand_id? number
---@field end_user_across_brand_requests? boolean
---@field end_user_upgrade_brand_association_behavior? string Controls how end users are associated with brands when upgraded to agents.
---@field new_agent_brand_association_behavior? string Controls how new agents are associated with brands. Determines the default brand assignment for newly created agents.
---@field require_brand_on_new_tickets? boolean

