---Messaging inactivity (capacity release) settings. See
---`settings_controller_support.rb` (`args_transformation_map['messaging_inactivity']`),
---`app/validators/messaging_inactivity_validator.rb`, and
---`settings_controller.rb#update`.
---@class zendesk.AccountSettingsMessagingInactivityInput
---@field enabled? boolean
---@field end_session? boolean
---@field reminders? zendesk.AccountSettingsMessagingInactivityInputRemindersList At most 3 reminders. Tags on each reminder are lower-cased, split on commas and whitespace, deduplicated and compacted before validation (`sanitize_tags`, `settings_controller.rb`). Then validated positionally by `MessagingInactivityValidator` — the array's index, not any field on the item, decides which fields are required: the first reminder (index 0) must omit both `timeout` and `ticket_status_id`; the second (index 1) must supply `timeout`; the third (index 2) must supply both `timeout` and a non-null `ticket_status_id`. A validation failure on any reminder renders a 400 for the whole request.
---@field ticket_status_id? number
---@field timeout? number Minutes. Enforced at the parameter gate as `3..15`.

---See the positional requirements on the parent `reminders` array — which
---fields are required depends on this item's position in the array, not on
---the item's own contents. `message` is the one exception: it is required
---at every position — the gate declares it `Parameters.string.required`,
---so a reminder without a `message` is rejected with a 400 before the
---positional validator runs.
---@class zendesk.AccountSettingsMessagingInactivityInputRemindersItem
---@field message string
---@field tags? zendesk.AccountSettingsMessagingInactivityInputRemindersItemTagsList
---@field ticket_status_id? number|distilled.Null The only property in this entire payload where an explicit `null` is genuinely accepted: the controller declares this parameter as `Parameters.integer | Parameters.nil` in the gate itself (`settings_controller.rb`), which is unaffected by the action's `forbid_nil_parameters` opt-in — that opt-in only disables the process-wide `allow_nil_for_everything` short-circuit, not an explicit `| Parameters.nil` declared on this one field. Null (or omission) is accepted for reminders at index 0 or 1; a reminder at index 2 that has a null or missing `ticket_status_id` fails `MessagingInactivityValidator`'s presence check with a 400.
---@field timeout? number Seconds (note: the top-level `timeout` sibling is minutes). Enforced at the parameter gate as `60..900`.

