---@class zendesk.AddOrganizationTagsRequest
---@field organization_id number The ID of an organization
---@field safe_update? boolean|distilled.Null Write only. When `true`, protects against ticket update collisions. Requires `updated_stamp`; sending `safe_update` without it returns a `409` on every resource. `false` has the same effect as omitting the property or sending `null`: no collision check is performed. Only affects the outcome for tickets. See [Protecting against ticket update collisions](/api-reference/ticketing/tickets/tickets/#protecting-against-ticket-update-collisions)
---@field tags? zendesk.AddOrganizationTagsRequestTags The tags to add to the ones already applied. An array of tag strings, or a single string. In either form each value is split on whitespace and on `,` `;` `|` `(` `)`, then stripped of special characters, downcased and de-duplicated. `null`, an empty array, an empty string and omitting the property are all accepted and leave the existing tags unchanged. Unlike the Set Tags operation, nothing here can clear a tag
---@field updated_stamp? string|distilled.Null Write only. The resource's last known `updated_at`. The update is applied only if it still matches, otherwise the request returns a `409`. `null` has the same effect as omitting the property: it is ignored unless `safe_update` is set, in which case the request returns a `409`. Only affects the outcome for tickets. See the `safe_update` property
---@field via? zendesk.AddOrganizationTagsRequestVia|distilled.Null Write only. `null` is accepted and treated as omitted. Only affects the outcome for tickets

