---that checks `status`, `type`, `group_id`, `assignee_id`, or `requester_id`.
---`null` leaves the stored conditions unchanged. An empty array `[]` is not the same thing: it
---builds an empty definition, which is rejected with a 422
---@alias zendesk.AutomationUpdateInputAllList zendesk.ConditionObject[]

---Logical OR conditions. Accepted as a top-level alternative to `conditions.any`.
---`null` leaves the stored conditions unchanged. An empty array `[]` is not the same thing: it
---builds an empty definition, which is rejected with a 422
---@alias zendesk.AutomationUpdateInputAnyList zendesk.ConditionObject[]

---`null` leaves the stored conditions unchanged. An empty object `{}` is not the same thing: it
---builds an empty definition, which is rejected with a 422. Neither is a `null` *inside* the
---object: `conditions.all` and `conditions.any` are folded into the top-level fields as
---`rule_params[:all] ||= conditions[:all] || []`, so a nested `null` becomes an empty condition
---set instead of being discarded, and an automation whose conditions are all cleared this way is
---rejected with the same 422
---@alias zendesk.AutomationUpdateInputConditions zendesk.ConditionsObject|any

---Who owns this automation. Set to `null` for the whole account. Not returned when reading an automation
