---@class zendesk.CurrentUserResponseUser
---@field active? boolean false if the user has been deleted
---@field agent_brand_ids? zendesk.CurrentUserResponseUserAgentBrandIdsList PUT or POST requests only. Assigns agent or agents to a brand. For more information, see [Agent brand ids](#agent-brand-ids)
---@field alias? string An alias displayed to end users
---@field chat_only? boolean Whether or not the user is a chat-only agent
---@field created_at? string The time the user was created
---@field custom_role_id? number|distilled.Null A custom role if the user is an agent on the Enterprise plan or above
---@field default_group_id? number The id of the user's default group
---@field details? string Any details you want to store about the user, such as an address
---@field email? string The user's primary email address. *Writeable on create only. On update, a secondary email is added. See [Email Address](#email-address)
---@field external_id? string|distilled.Null A unique identifier from another system. The API treats the id as case insensitive. Example: "ian1" and "IAN1" are the same value.
---@field iana_time_zone? string The time zone for the user
---@field id? number Automatically assigned when the user is created
---@field last_login_at? string Last time the user signed in to Zendesk Support or made an API request using an API token
---@field locale? string The user's locale. A BCP-47 compliant tag for the locale. If both "locale" and "locale_id" are present on create or update, "locale_id" is ignored and only "locale" is used.
---@field locale_id? number The user's language identifier
---@field moderator? boolean Designates whether the user has forum moderation capabilities
---@field name? string The user's name
---@field notes? string Any notes you want to store about the user
---@field only_private_comments? boolean true if the user can only create private comments
---@field organization_id? number|distilled.Null The id of the user's organization. If the user has more than one [organization memberships](/api-reference/ticketing/organizations/organization_memberships/), the id of the user's default organization. If updating, see [Organization ID](#organization-id)
---@field phone? string|distilled.Null The user's primary phone number. See [Phone Number](#phone-number) below
---@field photo? zendesk.CurrentUserResponseUserPhotoMap The user's profile picture represented as an [Attachment](/api-reference/ticketing/tickets/ticket-attachments/) object
---@field remote_photo_url? string A URL pointing to the user's profile picture.
---@field report_csv? boolean This parameter is inert and has no effect. It may be deprecated in the future. Previously, this parameter determined whether a user could access a CSV report in a legacy Guide dashboard. This dashboard has been removed. See [Announcing Guide legacy reporting upgrade to Explore](https://support.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4762263171610-Announcing-Guide-legacy-reporting-upgrade-to-Explore-)
---@field restricted_agent? boolean If the agent has any restrictions; false for admins and unrestricted agents, true for other agents
---@field role? string The user's role. Possible values are "end-user", "agent", or "admin"
---@field role_type? number|distilled.Null The user's role id. 0 for a custom agent, 1 for a light agent, 2 for a chat agent, 3 for a chat agent added to the Support account as a contributor ([Chat Phase 4](https://support.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4408836197658#topic_p1h_sx4_pgb)), 4 for an admin, and 5 for a billing admin
