---@class zendesk.CustomObjectFieldResponse
---@field custom_object_field? zendesk.CustomObjectField

---The writable attributes accepted when updating a custom object field. Every property is optional and an omitted property is left unchanged,
---with one exception: see the deletion warning on `custom_field_options`. `key` and `type` cannot be changed — `type` is filtered out of the
---request and a changed `key` is rejected with a validation error. On a standard field (`standard::name`, `standard::external_id`) only
---the title, description and properties may change (`raw_title` and `raw_description` are alternate routes to the title and description);
---anything else fails validation
---@class zendesk.CustomObjectFieldUpdateInputInput
---@field active? boolean Whether the field is available for use
---@field custom_field_options? zendesk.CustomObjectFieldUpdateInputInputCustomFieldOptionsList|distilled.Null For `dropdown` and `multiselect` fields only; sending it for any other field type is rejected. **The array replaces the whole option set: every option you omit is removed, and records referencing a removed option no longer resolve a value. An empty array removes every option.** So list all the options you want to keep, not just the ones you are changing. `null` and `[]` do opposite things here: `null` is ignored and leaves the option set exactly as it is, while `[]` deletes every option — both return a 200
---@field description? string A description of the field
---@field position? number The relative position of the field. Note that the [Reorder Custom Fields of an Object endpoint](#reorder-custom-fields-of-an-object) reassigns positions across every active field
---@field properties? zendesk.CustomObjectFieldUpdateInputInputProperties Field-specific properties, merged into the field's current properties: a property you omit keeps its current value, and omitting the whole object changes nothing. Only the properties that apply to this field's type are kept and the rest are **silently discarded** — the autonumbering and `is_unique` properties apply to the standard name field, `allowed_currencies` to `currency` fields, `cascade_permissions_enabled` to `parent` fields, and the roll-up properties to roll-up fields. Three of these are also account-gated and are only accepted when the feature is enabled on the account: the roll-up properties, `allowed_currencies` and `cascade_permissions_enabled`. Sending `allowed_currencies` without the currency feature is rejected outright. The autonumbering and `is_unique` properties cannot be changed once the object has any records. Use the top-level `required` property rather than `properties` to change whether a field is required. `null` in place of the whole object is accepted and changes nothing
---@field raw_description? string The dynamic content placeholder for the description, if the description is dynamic content. Takes precedence over `description`
---@field raw_title? string The dynamic content placeholder for the title, if the title is dynamic content. Takes precedence over `title`
---@field regexp_for_validation? string A pattern a field value must match to be valid. Honoured by `regexp` and `integer` fields
---@field relationship_filter? zendesk.CustomObjectFieldUpdateInputInputRelationshipFilter Narrows down the records the field can be set to. `null` is accepted and leaves the current filter in place
---@field required? boolean Whether the field must have a value when a record is created or updated. Stored as the `is_required` field property. Not editable on the standard name field, which is always required
---@field tag? string For `checkbox` fields only; sending it for any other field type is rejected. It has no tagging effect on a custom object field — custom object records are not tagged. Downcased before it is saved
---@field title? string The title of the field

---For `dropdown` and `multiselect` fields only; sending it for any other field type is rejected. **The array replaces the whole option
---set: every option you omit is removed, and records referencing a removed option no longer resolve a value. An empty array removes every
