---A new dynamic content item. There are two ways to give it a default variant: supply `default_locale_id` and `content` to
---create a single variant, or supply the `variants` array. `content` must not be combined with `variants`;
---`default_locale_id` may be sent alongside `variants` but is ignored.
---@class zendesk.DynamicContentInput
---@field content? string The content of the item's default variant. Use this together with `default_locale_id` as a shorthand for creating an item with a single variant. Required when `variants` is omitted — without it the default variant has no content and the request is rejected. **Must not be sent together with `variants`** — the two forms are mutually exclusive, and sending both returns a 400 `Invalid attribute` error whatever the value is.
---@field default_locale_id? number|distilled.Null The default locale of the item, which becomes the locale of its default variant. Must be one of the locales the account has active. Required unless `variants` is supplied, in which case this value is **ignored** and the default locale is taken from the variant whose `default` is `true`. A `null` is therefore only accepted alongside `variants`; without `variants` it is rejected.
---@field name string The unique name of the item. Must be unique within the account, must not contain non-ASCII characters and must not end in a hyphen. The item's `placeholder` is derived from it, and a name whose derived placeholder is already in use is also rejected.
---@field variants? zendesk.DynamicContentInputVariantsList|distilled.Null The variants to create for the item. Exactly one of them must have `default` set to `true`; if none does, the request is rejected because the item would have no default variant. Supplying this array makes `default_locale_id` inert, and `content` must not be sent alongside it. A `null` is treated as if the array were omitted, so the item is created from `default_locale_id` and `content` instead; an empty array is **not** equivalent and is rejected.

---The variants to create for the item. Exactly one of them must have `default` set to `true`; if none does, the
---request is rejected because the item would have no default variant. Supplying this array makes `default_locale_id`
---inert, and `content` must not be sent alongside it. A `null` is treated as if the array were omitted, so the item is
---created from `default_locale_id` and `content` instead; an empty array is **not** equivalent and is rejected.
---@alias zendesk.DynamicContentInputVariantsList zendesk.DynamicContentItemVariantInput[]

---A variant supplied in the `variants` array of a Create Item request. Create Item accepts a narrower set of attributes
---than the Item Variants API does, so this schema is not interchangeable with a standalone variant request body.
---@class zendesk.DynamicContentItemVariantInput
---@field content string The content of the variant. Evaluated as Liquid in the `dc` namespace, so it must be valid Liquid and must not reference the item's own placeholder. Cannot be blank.
---@field default? boolean|distilled.Null Whether this variant is the item's default variant. Exactly one variant in the array must set it to `true`, and the request is rejected if none does. Only the literal `true` counts — `null` and any other value are treated as `false`. If more than one variant sets it to `true`, only the last of them is stored as the default and the earlier ones are silently discarded.
---@field locale_id number The locale of the variant. Must be an existing locale id, and each locale may appear at most once per item.

---@class zendesk.DynamicContentListVariantsRequest
---@field dynamic_content_item_id number The ID of the dynamic content item
---@field page? zendesk.DynamicContentListVariantsRequestPage Pagination parameter. Supports both traditional offset and cursor-based pagination: - Traditional: `?page=2` (integer page number) - Cursor: `?page[size]=50&page[after]=cursor` (deepObject with size, after, before) These are mutually exclusive - use one format or the other, not both.
---@field per_page? number Number of records to return per page. Note: Default and maximum values vary by endpoint. Check endpoint-specific documentation for limits.
---@field sort? string Field to sort results by. Prefix with `-` for descending order. When used with cursor pagination, this determines the cursor ordering. Example: `?sort=name` or `?sort=-created_at`

---@alias zendesk.DynamicContentListVariantsRequestPage number|zendesk.DynamicContentListVariantsRequestPageCase1

---Cursor pagination parameters (JSON:API style)
---@class zendesk.DynamicContentListVariantsRequestPageCase1
---@field after? string Cursor token for next page
---@field before? string Cursor token for previous page
---@field size? number Number of records per page

---@class zendesk.DynamicContentObject
---@field created_at? string When this record was created
---@field default_locale_id number The default locale for the item. Must be one of the [locales the account has active](/api-reference/ticketing/account-configuration/locales/#list-locales).
---@field id? number Automatically assigned when creating items
---@field name string The unique name of the item
---@field outdated? boolean Indicates the item has outdated variants within it
---@field placeholder? string Automatically generated placeholder for the item, derived from name
