---@class zendesk.DynamicContentResponse
---@field item? zendesk.DynamicContentObject

---The item attributes to change. The name is the only attribute this endpoint can change; use the
---[Item Variants API](/api-reference/ticketing/ticket-management/dynamic_content_item_variants/) to add, update or delete
---variants. Sending no attributes is accepted and changes nothing.
---@class zendesk.DynamicContentUpdateInput
---@field name? string The new unique name of the item. Must be unique within the account, must not contain non-ASCII characters and must not end in a hyphen. The item's `placeholder` is **not** regenerated when the name changes — it keeps the value derived from the name the item was created with.

---A single variant to update. The update is partial — any omitted attribute is left unchanged. `locale_id` is not accepted: a variant's locale
---is fixed at creation, and sending it has no effect
---@class zendesk.DynamicContentVariantBulkUpdateItem
---@field active? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the variant is used when a user's locale matches it. Forced to `true` while the variant is the item's default, so `false` is silently ignored for that variant. `null` is accepted and stores no value, which reads the same as `false`
---@field content? string The content of the variant. Cannot be blank, and is parsed as a Liquid template: invalid Liquid is rejected, as is content that references its own item's `{{dc.<identifier>}}` placeholder
---@field default? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the variant is the item's default, used as the fallback when no variant matches the user's locale. Setting it to `true` demotes the item's previous default, and while a variant is the default it is always active and cannot be deleted. `null` is accepted and behaves the same as `false`
---@field id number The id of the variant to update. An item without it, or with an id that is not a variant of this item, fails that item alone rather than the request

---The writable attributes accepted when creating a dynamic content item variant
---@class zendesk.DynamicContentVariantInput
---@field active? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the variant is used when a user's locale matches it. Defaults to `true`, and is forced to `true` when the variant is the item's default. `null` is accepted and stores no value, which reads the same as `false`
---@field content string The content of the variant. Cannot be blank, and is parsed as a Liquid template: invalid Liquid is rejected, as is content that references its own item's `{{dc.<identifier>}}` placeholder
---@field default? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the variant is the item's default, used as the fallback when no variant matches the user's locale. Setting it to `true` demotes the item's previous default, and while a variant is the default it is always active and cannot be deleted. `null` is accepted and behaves the same as `false`
---@field locale_id number The id of the locale the variant provides content for. Must be an existing locale id, and only one variant per locale is allowed for an item — a second variant for the same locale is rejected. The locale of an existing variant cannot be changed

