---Only the supplied properties are updated. Each property is applied only when its value is present, so a
---blank or null value leaves the current value in place rather than clearing it, and an empty object is
---rejected. `filter` and `policy_metrics` are the exceptions: when either is supplied it **replaces** what
---the policy already has, so a partial value destroys the conditions or targets it leaves out
---@class zendesk.GroupSLAPolicyUpdateInput
---@field description? string|distilled.Null The description of the group SLA policy. A blank or null value is ignored, so the description cannot be cleared through this endpoint
---@field filter? zendesk.GroupSLAPolicyUpdateInputFilter The conditions a ticket must match. Supplying this **replaces the policy's conditions in full** — sending only `any` deletes the existing `all` conditions and vice versa, so a partial value destroys the conditions it omits. Omitting the property, or sending an empty object or a null value, leaves the existing conditions untouched
---@field policy_metrics? zendesk.GroupSLAPolicyUpdateInputPolicyMetricsList|distilled.Null The targets for the policy. See [Policy Metric](#policy-metric). Supplying this **replaces the policy's targets in full** — the existing targets are deleted and only the ones listed here survive, so a partial list destroys the targets it omits. Omitting the property, or sending an empty array or a null value, leaves the existing targets untouched
---@field position? number|distilled.Null Position of the group SLA policy, which determines the order policies are matched in. A null value is ignored
---@field title? string|distilled.Null The title of the group SLA policy. A blank or null value is ignored

---The conditions a ticket must match. Supplying this **replaces the policy's conditions in full** — sending only `any` deletes the existing `all` conditions and vice versa, so a partial value destroys the conditions it omits. Omitting the property, or sending an empty object or a null value, leaves the existing conditions untouched
---@alias zendesk.GroupSLAPolicyUpdateInputFilter zendesk.GroupSLAPolicyFilterInput|any

---The targets for the policy. See [Policy Metric](#policy-metric). Supplying this **replaces the policy's targets in full** — the existing targets are deleted and only the ones listed here survive, so a partial list destroys the targets it omits. Omitting the property, or sending an empty array or a null value, leaves the existing targets untouched
---@alias zendesk.GroupSLAPolicyUpdateInputPolicyMetricsList zendesk.GroupSLAPolicyMetricInput[]

