---@field organization zendesk.OrganizationBulkUpdateInput

---Organization attributes to create with, or to apply to the matched organization. Matching is by `id` first and then by `external_id`; when neither matches, a new organization is created from these attributes and `name` becomes mandatory. When an organization is matched, every property is optional and omitting one leaves the stored value unchanged — but see the per-property notes, as several properties replace the stored value wholesale rather than merging into it.
---@class zendesk.OrganizationCreateOrUpdateInput
---@field details? string|distilled.Null Any details about the organization, such as the address. `null` clears the stored value.
---@field domain_names? zendesk.OrganizationCreateOrUpdateInputDomainNames Domain names and email addresses to associate with this organization. Accepts either an array of values or a single string of values separated by commas, semicolons or spaces. **Destructive on a matched organization:** the supplied list replaces the stored list wholesale, so every omitted domain and email is deleted; `null`, an empty array and an empty string all clear them all. Omit the property entirely to leave the stored list untouched.
---@field external_id? zendesk.OrganizationCreateOrUpdateInputExternalId A unique external id to associate the organization to an external record. Used as the second matching criterion: when `id` matches nothing, a case-insensitive match on `external_id` selects the organization to update, so "company1" and "Company1" are considered the same. `null` or an empty string skips the match and clears the stored value; a value already used by another organization returns 422.
---@field group_id? number|distilled.Null New tickets from users in this organization are automatically put in this group. `null` unassigns the group.
---@field id? zendesk.OrganizationCreateOrUpdateInputId The id of an existing organization to update. Accepts an integer or its decimal string form. If no organization has this id, matching falls back to `external_id`; only when neither matches is a new organization created. Omit it, or send `null`, to match on `external_id` alone.
---@field name? string A unique name for the organization. **Mandatory when creating** — if neither `id` nor `external_id` matches an existing organization, omitting it fails with 422. Optional when an existing organization is matched. Cannot contain the `|` character and must be unique within the account; a duplicate returns 422. Cannot be cleared — an empty string or `null` fails the presence validation with 422.
---@field notes? string|distilled.Null Any notes you have about the organization. `null` clears the stored value. This is the only attribute applied for an agent restricted to `edit_notes` on a matched organization; for such an agent every other attribute here is silently ignored and the request still returns 200. `organization_fields` is the exception — it is applied for a restricted agent too. **Destructive exception:** for a caller without `edit` permission on organizations this is the only attribute applied, and it is assigned unconditionally — omitting `notes` on a matched organization clears the stored value (when `ocp_org_create_or_update_require_edit` is disabled; with it enabled such callers get 403 before matching).
---@field organization_fields? zendesk.OrganizationCreateOrUpdateInputOrganizationFieldsMap|distilled.Null Custom organization field values, keyed by field key. See [Custom organization fields](/api-reference/ticketing/organizations/organizations/#custom-organization-fields). Only keys matching an existing organization field take effect; unknown keys are silently ignored. Supplied keys are merged into the stored values, so omitted keys keep their value, and a `null` or blank value for a key deletes that field's stored value. `null` for the whole map is accepted and changes nothing. Requires the `user_and_organization_fields` account feature; without it the whole map is silently ignored.
---@field shared_comments? boolean End users in this organization are able to comment on each other's tickets. An explicit `null` is rejected with 400. Only takes effect when `shared_tickets` is `true` — the model resets it to `false` whenever the organization is not sharing tickets.
---@field shared_tickets? boolean End users in this organization are able to see each other's tickets. An explicit `null` is rejected with 400. Setting this to `false` also forces `shared_comments` to `false`. Deprecated in favor of `ticket_restriction`, which takes precedence when both are sent in the same request: `shared_tickets` is then silently dropped from the request and, when the two contradict, the response carries a top-level `warnings` array saying so (this precedence behavior requires the `enable_sync_ticket_restriction` account feature). Sent on its own, it still applies: when the `enable_sync_ticket_restriction` account feature is enabled, the stored `ticket_restriction` is synchronized to `organization` for `true` or `restricted` for `false`; with the feature disabled a non-null stored `ticket_restriction` is left unchanged (a stored `null` always reads as derived from `shared_tickets`).
---@field tags? zendesk.OrganizationCreateOrUpdateInputTags The tags of the organization. Accepts either an array of tags or a single string of space-separated tags. Requires the `user_and_organization_tags` account feature; without it the value is accepted and silently ignored. **Destructive on a matched organization:** the supplied list replaces the stored list wholesale, so every omitted tag is deleted; `null`, an empty array and an empty string all remove every tag. Omit the property entirely to leave the stored tags untouched.
---@field ticket_restriction? zendesk.OrganizationCreateOrUpdateInputTicketRestriction|string|distilled.Null Which tickets end users in this organization can see. `restricted` hides each end user's tickets from the other end users in the organization; `organization` lets them see each other's tickets; `organization_and_descendants` extends that to end users in descendant organizations and requires the organization hierarchy to be enabled on the account, otherwise it is rejected with 422. Any other value is rejected with 422. `null` clears the stored restriction, which then derives from `shared_tickets`. Takes precedence over `shared_tickets` — see that property for what happens when both are sent.

