---Organization attributes to update. Every property is optional and omitting one leaves the stored value unchanged, but see the per-property notes: several properties replace the stored value wholesale rather than merging into it. An empty object is accepted and changes nothing.
---@class zendesk.OrganizationUpdateInput
---@field details? string|distilled.Null Any details about the organization, such as the address. `null` clears the stored value.
---@field domain_names? zendesk.OrganizationUpdateInputDomainNames Domain names and email addresses to associate with this organization. Accepts either an array of values or a single string of values separated by commas, semicolons or spaces. **Destructive:** the supplied list replaces the stored list wholesale, so every omitted domain and email is deleted; `null`, an empty array and an empty string all clear them all. Omit the property entirely to leave the stored list untouched.
---@field external_id? zendesk.OrganizationUpdateInputExternalId A unique external id to associate the organization to an external record. The id is case-insensitive, so "company1" and "Company1" are considered the same. `null` or an empty string clears it; a value already used by another organization returns 422.
---@field group_id? number|distilled.Null New tickets from users in this organization are automatically put in this group. `null` unassigns the group.
---@field name? string A unique name for the organization. Cannot contain the `|` character and must be unique within the account; a duplicate returns 422. Cannot be cleared — an empty string or `null` fails the presence validation with 422.
---@field notes? string|distilled.Null Any notes you have about the organization. `null` clears the stored value for a caller with `edit` permission; for an agent restricted to `edit_notes`, `null` is ignored and the stored notes are left untouched — only a non-empty value (including an empty string) is assigned. This is the only attribute an agent restricted to `edit_notes` can change; for such an agent every other attribute here is silently ignored and the request still returns 200. `organization_fields` is the exception — it is applied for a restricted agent too, unless the account has `up_restrict_organization_field_updates` enabled.
---@field organization_fields? zendesk.OrganizationUpdateInputOrganizationFieldsMap|distilled.Null Custom organization field values, keyed by field key. See [Custom organization fields](/api-reference/ticketing/organizations/organizations/#custom-organization-fields). Only keys matching an existing organization field take effect; unknown keys are silently ignored. Supplied keys are merged into the stored values, so omitted keys keep their value, and a `null` or blank value for a key deletes that field's stored value. `null` for the whole map is accepted and changes nothing. Requires the `user_and_organization_fields` account feature; without it the whole map is silently ignored, as it also is for agents without `edit` permission on organizations when the account has `up_restrict_organization_field_updates` enabled.
---@field shared_comments? boolean End users in this organization are able to comment on each other's tickets. An explicit `null` is rejected with 400. Only takes effect when `shared_tickets` is `true` — the model resets it to `false` whenever the organization is not sharing tickets.
---@field shared_tickets? boolean End users in this organization are able to see each other's tickets. An explicit `null` is rejected with 400. Setting this to `false` also forces `shared_comments` to `false`. Deprecated in favor of `ticket_restriction`, which takes precedence when both are sent in the same request: `shared_tickets` is then silently dropped from the request and, when the two contradict, the response carries a top-level `warnings` array saying so (this precedence behavior requires the `enable_sync_ticket_restriction` account feature). Sent on its own, it still applies: when the `enable_sync_ticket_restriction` account feature is enabled, the stored `ticket_restriction` is synchronized to `organization` for `true` or `restricted` for `false`; with the feature disabled a non-null stored `ticket_restriction` is left unchanged (a stored `null` always reads as derived from `shared_tickets`).
---@field tags? zendesk.OrganizationUpdateInputTags The tags of the organization. Accepts either an array of tags or a single string of space-separated tags. Requires the `user_and_organization_tags` account feature; without it the value is accepted and silently ignored. **Destructive:** the supplied list replaces the stored list wholesale, so every omitted tag is deleted; `null`, an empty array and an empty string all remove every tag. Omit the property entirely to leave the stored tags untouched.
---@field ticket_restriction? zendesk.OrganizationUpdateInputTicketRestriction|string|distilled.Null Which tickets end users in this organization can see. `restricted` hides each end user's tickets from the other end users in the organization; `organization` lets them see each other's tickets; `organization_and_descendants` extends that to end users in descendant organizations and requires the organization hierarchy to be enabled on the account, otherwise it is rejected with 422. Any other value is rejected with 422. `null` clears the stored restriction, which then derives from `shared_tickets`. Takes precedence over `shared_tickets` — see that property for what happens when both are sent.

---Domain names and email addresses to associate with this organization. Accepts either an array of values or a single string of values separated by commas, semicolons or spaces. **Destructive:** the supplied list replaces the stored list wholesale, so every omitted domain and email is deleted; `null`, an empty array and an empty string all clear them all. Omit the property entirely to leave the stored list untouched.
