---@field end_user boolean If true, the method is used for the end-user remote authentication
---@field end_user_primary boolean If end users for sign-in are redirected to a remote authentication, this is the default method shown to an end user
---@field fingerprint? string For the "saml" auth mode only. The SHA-256 certificate fingerprint.
---@field id? number Uniquely identifies a remote authentication. Automatically assigned on creation
---@field ip_ranges? string|distilled.Null Requests from these IP ranges will always be routed via remote authentication. Requests from IP addresses outside these ranges will be routed to the normal sign-in form. When this is blank, all requests are routed through remote authentication. An IP range is in the format n.n.n.n, where n is a number or an asterisk (*) wild card. Multiple IP ranges are separated with spaces
---@field is_active? boolean If true, the method is enabled for end users or team members
---@field issuer_url? string For the "oidc" auth mode only. This is the URL that is used as the logical identifier for your provider's connection
---@field jwks_url? string For the "oidc" auth mode only. This is the URL that returns the provider's JSON Web Key Set
