---@field priority? number
---@field remote_login_url string The URL that Zendesk invokes to redirect users to the identity provider
---@field remote_logout_url string The URL that Zendesk uses to redirect users after they sign out. Supported authentication types: SAML, JWT. Not supported for OIDC
---@field scope? string For the "oidc" auth mode only. These are the user details your account can access, like name and email address. Supported scopes within the OIDC standard include `openid`, `profile`, `email`, `address`, and `phone`. It must contain at least `openid` and `email`. Scopes are separated with spaces
---@field token_url? string For the "oidc" auth mode only. Your account uses this URL to request access tokens for users
---@field update_external_ids? boolean For the "jwt" auth mode only. When enabled, the external id of the user being signed in can be updated. This only happens when a user with the external id is not found, but the user's email address is found. The external id is unique for an account. Users without an external id will have one added if it is present in the authentication request
---@field user_info_url? string For the "oidc" auth mode only. This the URL that returns Claims about the authenticated user

