---The comment to add to the request. On Create Request the comment is mandatory and supplies the request's read-only
---`description`. A comment carrying `uploads` but no text is rejected on both operations. Comments added through this
---endpoint always take the publicity the account computes for the caller; an end user cannot choose it here.
---@class zendesk.RequestCommentInput
---@field body? string|distilled.Null The comment text, as Zendesk markdown. Takes precedence over `value`, but is overridden by `html_body` when both are sent. On create this becomes the request's `description`
---@field html_body? string|distilled.Null The comment text as HTML. Takes precedence over both `body` and `value` whenever it is sent, and stores the comment in rich-text format
---@field uploads? zendesk.RequestCommentInputUploads One or more attachment upload tokens to attach to the comment. Blank tokens are discarded, and both a null and an empty array are discarded entirely, leaving the comment with no new attachments. On an anonymous create the number of attachments is capped by the account's anonymous attachment limit
---@field value? string|distilled.Null A legacy alias for `body`, applied only when `body` is absent, and likewise overridden by `html_body`

---One or more attachment upload tokens to attach to the comment. Blank tokens are discarded, and both a null and an
---empty array are discarded entirely, leaving the comment with no new attachments. On an anonymous create the number
