---The properties an end user may change on an existing request: a comment, the solved flag, collaborators and the
---organization. Every other request attribute is read-only once the request exists, and the properties accepted only on
---create are not accepted here.
---@class zendesk.RequestUpdateInput
---@field additional_collaborators? zendesk.RequestUpdateInputAdditionalCollaborators Collaborators (CCs) to add to the request, as user ids, email addresses, or objects carrying a name and an email. Existing collaborators are kept. Only applied when the account allows collaborators. At most 48 collaborators may be sent in one call on accounts with CCs and followers enabled, and null is ignored
---@field comment? zendesk.RequestUpdateInputComment The comment to add. Null and an empty object are both accepted and add no comment
---@field email_ccs? zendesk.RequestUpdateInputEmailCcsList|distilled.Null Email CCs to add to or remove from the request, up to 48 entries with `action: "put"` per call. Each entry is applied on its own and CCs that are not listed are left untouched, so null and an empty array both leave the CC list unchanged. On an account without CCs and followers enabled the `put` entries are still applied, as plain collaborators; only `delete` entries need the feature
---@field organization_id? number|distilled.Null The id of the organization to associate the request with. Applied for the requester, who may always edit their own request's properties. Unlike on create there is no silent substitution here: an organization the requester does not belong to **fails the update** with a 422 and `organization_id is not a valid organization for the requester`. Null is replaced by the requester's default organization, if they have one
---@field safe_update? boolean|distilled.Null Set to true to make the update conditional on `updated_stamp` still matching the request's `updated_at`. Null is ignored
---@field solved? boolean|distilled.Null Set to true to solve the request. Only applied when the request is assigned to an agent, which the request's read-only `can_be_solved_by_me` property reports. Null is ignored
---@field system_metadata? zendesk.RequestUpdateInputSystemMetadata|distilled.Null Client and IP information to store as system metadata on the update's audit. Accepted from any caller but only applied for internal Zendesk services, and a null is ignored
---@field updated_stamp? string|distilled.Null The request's last known `updated_at`, used with `safe_update` to reject the update if the request has changed since. Null is ignored
---@field via? zendesk.RequestUpdateInputVia The channel the update came through

