---@field id? number Automatically assigned upon creation
---@field reason? string The reason for a bad rating given by the requester in a follow-up question. Satisfaction reasons must be [enabled](https://support.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4408886173338)
---@field reason_code? number The default reasons the user can select from a list menu for giving a negative rating. See [Reason codes](/api-reference/ticketing/ticket-management/satisfaction_reasons/#reason-codes) in the Satisfaction Reasons API. Can only be set on ratings with a `score` of "bad". Responses don't include this property
---@field reason_id? number id for the reason the user gave a negative rating. Can only be set on ratings with a `score` of "bad". To get a descriptive value for the id, use the [Show Reason for Satisfaction Rating](/api-reference/ticketing/ticket-management/satisfaction_reasons/#show-reason-for-satisfaction-rating) endpoint
---@field requester_id number The id of ticket requester submitting the rating
---@field score string The rating "offered", "unoffered", "good" or "bad". For POST requests, only "good" or "bad" are valid
---@field ticket_id number The id of ticket being rated
---@field updated_at? string The time the satisfaction rating got updated
---@field url? string The API url of this rating

