---@field brand_id? zendesk.SearchUsersRequestBrandId When brand separation is enabled, scopes the search to users belonging to the specified brand. Only applicable when the account has brand separation enabled. Accepted values: * "all" — search all users across all brands (no brand filtering applied). * 0 — restrict the search to account-scoped (brand-less) users only. * A numeric brand id — if the brand has user separation enabled, search returns end users belonging to that brand plus the agents with membership in that brand and all admins. If the brand does not have user separation enabled, the request falls back to account scope (0). If `brand_id` is omitted, the account's `brand_user_separation_scope_query_default` [brand setting](/api-reference/ticketing/account-configuration/account_settings/#brands) decides the scope. If it's set to `"error"`, the request is rejected with `400 Bad Request`. Agent Workspace, other signed-in Zendesk sessions and internal Zendesk requests always use `all`. The resolved scope is returned in the `X-Zendesk-Brand-Id-Scope-Resolved` response header.
