---The writable attributes accepted when creating a sharing agreement.
---@class zendesk.SharingAgreementCreateInput
---@field allows_public_comments? boolean Whether the remote account may add public comments to the shared ticket and keep its status in sync. When `false`, public comments arriving from the remote account are **discarded** rather than imported — they are not stored as private comments — and ticket status is neither sent to nor accepted from the remote account. Even when `true`, an account setting can separately suppress a remote request to close the ticket. Defaults to `false` when omitted. Like `sync_tags`, this value is only communicated to the remote account with the initial invitation and cannot be changed later through the API.
---@field remote_subdomain string The subdomain of the Zendesk account you want to share tickets with. The account must already exist — an unrecognized or blank subdomain is rejected, as is your own subdomain. This is the only way to identify the remote party through this endpoint, so agreements created here are always Zendesk-to-Zendesk and always outbound; agreements with Jira or another third party can only be created in the admin interface. The new agreement is created with `status` `pending` and an invitation is sent to the remote account, which must accept it before tickets can be shared.
---@field sync_custom_fields? boolean Whether custom field values are copied between the local ticket and its shared copy on the remote account. Fields are matched by title, so a value is only applied on either side if a ticket field with the same title exists there. Defaults to `false` when omitted. Like `sync_tags`, this value is only communicated to the remote account with the initial invitation and cannot be changed later through the API.
---@field sync_tags? boolean Whether tags are copied between the local ticket and its shared copy on the remote account. Defaults to `false` when omitted. This value is only communicated to the remote account with the initial invitation, so it cannot be changed later through the API — only `status` is updatable.

---A sharing agreement configuration to apply to a ticket
---@class zendesk.SharingAgreementInput
---@field custom_fields? zendesk.SharingAgreementInputCustomFieldsList
---@field id? number The ID of the sharing agreement

