---@field additional_collaborators? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputAdditionalCollaboratorsList Write only. An array of numeric IDs, emails, or objects containing name and email properties. See [Setting Collaborators](/api-reference/ticketing/tickets/tickets/#setting-collaborators). An email notification is sent to them when the ticket is updated
---@field assignee_email? string Write only. The email address of the agent to assign the ticket to
---@field assignee_id? number|distilled.Null The agent currently assigned to the ticket
---@field attribute_value_ids? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputAttributeValueIdsList Write only. An array of the IDs of attribute values to be associated with the ticket
---@field brand_id? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputBrandId|distilled.Null The id of the brand this ticket is associated with. See [Setting up multiple brands](https://support.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4408829476378)
---@field collaborator_ids? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputCollaboratorIdsList The ids of users currently CC'ed on the ticket
---@field collaborators? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputCollaboratorsList Write only. Users to add as cc's when creating a ticket. See [Setting Collaborators](/documentation/ticketing/managing-tickets/creating-and-updating-tickets#setting-collaborators)
---@field comment? zendesk.TicketCommentObjectInput
---@field custom_fields? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputCustomFieldsList Custom field values to set on the ticket. Each entry specifies a field ID and its value. See [Setting custom field values](/documentation/ticketing/managing-tickets/creating-and-updating-tickets#setting-custom-field-values)
---@field custom_status_id? number|distilled.Null The custom ticket status id of the ticket. See [custom ticket statuses](#custom-ticket-statuses)
---@field description? string The first comment on the ticket. When [creating a ticket](#create-ticket), use `comment` to set the description. See [Description and first comment](#description-and-first-comment). On create, can be set directly as an alternative to `comment`. Silently ignored on update.
---@field due_at? string|distilled.Null If this is a ticket of type "task" it has a due date. Due date format uses [ISO 8601](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) format
---@field email_ccs? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputEmailCcsList|distilled.Null Write only. An array of objects that represent agent or end users email CCs to add or delete from the ticket. See [Setting email CCs](/documentation/ticketing/managing-tickets/creating-and-updating-tickets/#setting-email-ccs). Ignored when [CCs and followers](https://support.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4408822451482) is not enabled
---@field external_id? string|distilled.Null An id you can use to link Zendesk Support tickets to local records
---@field fields? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputFieldsList Alias for custom_fields. Custom field values to set on the ticket. Each entry specifies a field ID and its value.
---@field followers? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputFollowersList Write only. An array of objects that represents agent followers to add or delete from the ticket. See [Setting followers](/documentation/ticketing/managing-tickets/creating-and-updating-tickets/#setting-followers). Ignored when [CCs and followers](https://support.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4408822451482) is not enabled
---@field forum_topic_id? number The topic in the Zendesk Web portal this ticket originated from, if any. The Web portal is deprecated
---@field group_id? number|distilled.Null The group this ticket is assigned to
---@field macro_id? number Write only. A single macro ID to be recorded in the ticket audit
---@field macro_ids? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputMacroIdsList Write only. List of macro IDs to be recorded in the ticket audit
---@field metadata? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputMetadataMap Write only. Metadata for the audit. In the `audit` object, the data is specified in the `custom` property of the `metadata` object. See [Setting Metadata](/documentation/ticketing/managing-tickets/creating-and-updating-tickets/#setting-metadata)
---@field organization_id? number|distilled.Null The organization of the requester. You can only specify the ID of an organization associated with the requester. See [Organization Memberships](/api-reference/ticketing/organizations/organization_memberships/)
---@field origin_zrn? string Write only. The Zendesk Resource Name (ZRN) of the origin for this ticket
---@field priority? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputPriority|string|distilled.Null The urgency with which the ticket should be addressed
---@field problem_id? number|distilled.Null For tickets of type "incident", the ID of the problem the incident is linked to
---@field raw_subject? string The dynamic content placeholder, if present, or the "subject" value, if not. See [Dynamic Content Items](/api-reference/ticketing/ticket-management/dynamic_content/). When set on create or update, overrides the `subject` field.
---@field recipient? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputRecipient The original recipient e-mail address of the ticket. Notification emails for the ticket are sent from this address
---@field requester? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputRequester Write only. Alternative to requester_id for specifying the ticket requester. Can be provided as: - Email string: "user@example.com" - User ID integer: 12345 - User object: {name: "John Doe", email: "john@example.com"} If both requester and requester_id are provided, requester_id takes precedence. When creating a ticket, if the user doesn't exist, they may be created automatically depending on account settings.
---@field requester_id? number|distilled.Null The user who requested this ticket
---@field safe_update? boolean Write only. Optional boolean. When true and an `updated_stamp` date is included, protects against ticket update collisions and returns a message to let you know if one occurs. See [Protecting against ticket update collisions](/documentation/ticketing/managing-tickets/creating-and-updating-tickets/#protecting-against-ticket-update-collisions). A value of false has the same effect as true. Omit the property to force the updates to not be safe
---@field sharing_agreement_ids? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputSharingAgreementIdsList An array of the numeric IDs of sharing agreements. Note that this replaces any existing agreements
---@field sharing_agreements? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputSharingAgreements Write only. Sharing agreement configuration for the ticket. Accepts a single object or an array of objects.
---@field status? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputStatus|string The state of the ticket. If your account has activated custom ticket statuses, this is the ticket's status category. See [custom ticket statuses](#custom-ticket-statuses)
---@field subject? string|distilled.Null The value of the subject field for this ticket. See [Subject](/api-reference/ticketing/tickets/tickets/#subject)
---@field submitter_id? number|distilled.Null The user who submitted the ticket. The submitter always becomes the author of the first comment on the ticket. If not specified, defaults to the authenticated user.
---@field support_type? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputSupportType|string|distilled.Null The type of support that handled the ticket
---@field suspended_ticket_id? number Write only. The ID of the suspended ticket being recovered
---@field suspension_type_id? number Write only. The suspension type ID when recovering a suspended ticket
---@field system_metadata? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputSystemMetadata Write only. System metadata for the ticket, typically set by internal clients
---@field tags? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputTags The tags applied to this ticket. Unless otherwise specified, the [set tag](/api-reference/ticketing/ticket-management/tags/#set-tags) behavior is used, which overwrites and replaces existing tags
---@field tde_workspace? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputTdeWorkspace Write only. TDE workspace information for the ticket
---@field ticket_form_id? number|distilled.Null Enterprise only. The id of the ticket form to render for the ticket
---@field tpe_voice_comment? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputTpeVoiceComment Write only. A TPE voice comment for Talk Partner Edition tickets
---@field type? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputType|string|distilled.Null The type of this ticket
---@field updated_stamp? string Write only. Datetime of last update received from API. See the `safe_update` property
---@field via_followup_source_id? number Write only. The id of a closed ticket when creating a follow-up ticket. See [Creating a follow-up ticket](/documentation/ticketing/managing-tickets/creating-and-updating-tickets#creating-a-follow-up-ticket)
---@field via_id? number Write only. For more information, see the [Via object reference](/documentation/ticketing/reference-guides/via-object-reference/)
---@field voice_comment? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputVoiceComment Write only. A voice comment for Talk tickets. See [Adding voice comments to tickets](/documentation/ticketing/managing-tickets/adding-voice-comments-to-tickets/)
---@field additional_tags? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputAdditionalTagsList An array of tags to add to the ticket
---@field remove_tags? zendesk.TicketCreateVoicemailTicketInputInputRemoveTagsList An array of tags to remove from the ticket

