---@class zendesk.TicketFormAgentConditionObjectChildFieldsItemRequiredOnStatuses
---@field custom_statuses? zendesk.TicketFormAgentConditionObjectChildFieldsItemRequiredOnStatusesCustomStatusesList For `SOME_STATUSES` only, and only on accounts with custom ticket statuses enabled — otherwise ignored. The IDs of the custom statuses the field is required on. Cannot be combined with `statuses`
---@field statuses? zendesk.TicketFormAgentConditionObjectChildFieldsItemRequiredOnStatusesStatusesList|distilled.Null For `SOME_STATUSES` only. The system statuses the field is required on. Cannot be combined with `custom_statuses` — on accounts with custom ticket statuses enabled sending both is rejected, and on other accounts `custom_statuses` is ignored. A null counts as sending the attribute for that rejection, and otherwise behaves like an empty array: the condition is stored as `NO_STATUSES`
---@field type? zendesk.TicketFormAgentConditionObjectChildFieldsItemRequiredOnStatusesType|string|distilled.Null `ALL_STATUSES` requires the field on every status, `NO_STATUSES` on none, and `SOME_STATUSES` requires the field only on the statuses listed in `statuses` or `custom_statuses`. A `SOME_STATUSES` object carrying neither list is stored as `NO_STATUSES`. Omitting the type, or sending null, is also stored as `NO_STATUSES`

