---@class zendesk.TicketFormTicketFormStatusesRequest
---@field ticket_form_id number The ID of the ticket form

---The writable attributes accepted when updating a ticket form. Every attribute is optional and an omitted attribute is
---left unchanged, but `ticket_field_ids`, `restricted_brand_ids`, `agent_conditions` and `end_user_conditions` are
---replaced wholesale rather than merged — see each description. A form's `form_type` cannot be changed after creation.
---@class zendesk.TicketFormUpdateInput
---@field active? boolean Whether the form is available for use. The default form cannot be made inactive
---@field agent_conditions? zendesk.TicketFormUpdateInputAgentConditionsList|distilled.Null The complete set of condition sets for the agent interface. Any existing agent condition not restated in the array is deleted, so send the full list. Passing an empty array or null deletes them all
---@field default? boolean Whether this is the account's default form. Setting it forces `end_user_visible` to true, demotes the previous default form, and is rejected for a `service_catalog` form or an inactive form. The current default form cannot clear its own flag — promote another form instead
---@field display_name? string|distilled.Null The name of the form shown to end users. Sending null clears it, but only on a form that is not end-user visible — on an end-user-visible form a null is rejected, and when the same request also sets `end_user_visible` the null is replaced by `name`
---@field end_user_conditions? zendesk.TicketFormUpdateInputEndUserConditionsList|distilled.Null The complete set of condition sets for end-user products. Any existing end-user condition not restated in the array is deleted, so send the full list. Passing an empty array or null deletes them all
---@field end_user_visible? boolean Whether the form is visible to end users. Always true for the default form
---@field in_all_brands? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the form is available in every brand on this account. A null value is ignored rather than applied
---@field name? string The name of the form
---@field position? number The position of this form among the account's other forms. Unlike a create, an update will not default it: a null is rejected because a live form must have a position
---@field raw_display_name? string|distilled.Null A dynamic content placeholder for the display name. Takes the place of `display_name` when both are given, including when it is an empty string. See [Dynamic Content](/api-reference/ticketing/ticket-management/dynamic_content/). Sending null is accepted and discarded: `display_name` is left as sent
---@field raw_name? string|distilled.Null A dynamic content placeholder for the name. Takes the place of `name` when both are given, including when it is an empty string. See [Dynamic Content](/api-reference/ticketing/ticket-management/dynamic_content/). Sending null is accepted and discarded: `name` is left as sent
---@field restricted_brand_ids? zendesk.TicketFormUpdateInputRestrictedBrandIdsList|distilled.Null The complete set of brands this form is restricted to. Any brand currently restricting the form whose ID is absent from the array is removed, so send the full list rather than a partial one. Passing an empty array or null removes every restriction. IDs that do not name an active brand on the account are silently dropped. Only applied on accounts with more than one active brand
---@field ticket_field_ids? zendesk.TicketFormUpdateInputTicketFieldIdsList|distilled.Null The complete, ordered set of ticket fields on this form. Any field currently on the form whose ID is absent from the array is REMOVED from the form, so a partial list silently drops fields — send the full list, or omit the attribute entirely to leave the form's fields untouched. An empty array and null are also treated as omitted and cannot be used to clear the form. The account's system-required fields are prepended automatically

---The complete set of condition sets for the agent interface. Any existing agent condition not restated in the array
---is deleted, so send the full list. Passing an empty array or null deletes them all
---@alias zendesk.TicketFormUpdateInputAgentConditionsList zendesk.TicketFormAgentConditionObject[]

---The complete set of condition sets for end-user products. Any existing end-user condition not restated in the
---array is deleted, so send the full list. Passing an empty array or null deletes them all
---@alias zendesk.TicketFormUpdateInputEndUserConditionsList zendesk.TicketFormEndUserConditionObject[]

---The complete set of brands this form is restricted to. Any brand currently restricting the form whose ID is absent
---from the array is removed, so send the full list rather than a partial one. Passing an empty array or null removes
---every restriction. IDs that do not name an active brand on the account are silently dropped. Only applied on
---accounts with more than one active brand
---@alias zendesk.TicketFormUpdateInputRestrictedBrandIdsList number[]

---The complete, ordered set of ticket fields on this form. Any field currently on the form whose ID is absent from
---the array is REMOVED from the form, so a partial list silently drops fields — send the full list, or omit the
---attribute entirely to leave the form's fields untouched. An empty array and null are also treated as omitted and
---cannot be used to clear the form. The account's system-required fields are prepended automatically
---@alias zendesk.TicketFormUpdateInputTicketFieldIdsList number[]

