---@alias zendesk.TrialAccountAddressInputPhone string|number

---An additional agent to create in the new account. Corresponds to `Api::V2::AccountsController::AGENTS_PARAMETER`.
---@class zendesk.TrialAccountAgentInput
---@field email? string The agent's email address.
---@field name? string The agent's full name.
---@field role? string The agent's role, for example `Admin` or `Agent`. Not validated by this controller.

---Attributes of the trial account to provision. Corresponds to `Api::V2::AccountsController::ACCOUNT_PARAMETER`.
---@class zendesk.TrialAccountInput
---@field _zd_choose_shard_udupi? number|distilled.Null Preferred database shard for the new account. Formerly read by `Zendesk::Accounts::Initializer` on the Classic creation path, which PLATOPS-1372 removed; the value is now accepted and forwarded verbatim, and whether the account service honours it is outside this repository.
---@field currency? string|distilled.Null Currency code for the account.
---@field employee_service_suite_trial? zendesk.TrialAccountInputEmployeeServiceSuiteTrial Provisions an Employee Service Suite trial (a professional-plan `employee_service_suite` SKU expiring in 14 days) with `account.account_type` set to `pre_spp`. Enabled by any value the parameter gate coerces to true (`1`, `"1"`, `true`, `"true"`, `"on"`). Takes effect only when `zendesk_suite_trial` is not set, which is evaluated first.
---@field google_apps_domain? string|distilled.Null Google Workspace domain to associate with the account. Must not already be routed to another account and must not be `gmail.com`; either returns `409 Conflict`.
---@field help_desk_size? string|distilled.Null Free-form description of the expected number of agents, for example `Small Team`, `1-9` or `Large group`. Surfaced verbatim as `company_size` in the signup tracking properties (`Account::Tracking`); any categorisation happens downstream of this repository. Not enforced by this controller's own gates; `Account` validates its presence on create, but the record is created by the account service, out of process. `null` and omission are indistinguishable here.
---@field language? string|distilled.Null Locale for the new account, for example `ja`. Copied to `account.locale` before the payload is forwarded.
---@field multiproduct? zendesk.TrialAccountInputMultiproduct Legacy switch for the account's product configuration. PLATOPS-1372 removed the multiproduct branch and the legacy Classic fallback from `create`, so this controller no longer reads the value and it has no effect on which service handles the request. It is still accepted by the parameter gate and forwarded verbatim to the account service like every other permitted property; whether it affects provisioning is decided by the account service, outside this repository. The value the account service returns is echoed back as `account.multiproduct` in the response body.
---@field name? string|distilled.Null The name of the account. Not enforced by this controller's own gates; accepted and forwarded to the account service, which decides whether it is required. `null` and omission are indistinguishable here.
---@field remote_authentication? zendesk.TrialAccountInputRemoteAuthentication Single sign-on configuration for the new account. Accepted and forwarded to the account service verbatim; this controller does not read it.
---@field remote_login_url? string|distilled.Null Remote login URL for the account. Distinct from `remote_authentication.remote_login_url`; both are accepted and forwarded.
---@field source? string|distilled.Null Provisioning channel this signup came from. Also copied into `trial_extras.source` when present.
---@field subdomain string The subdomain to provision, and the only place this controller looks for it. Must match `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{1,}[a-z0-9]$` (`SUBDOMAIN_PATTERN`, lib/vars.rb), must not start with `xn--`, and must be neither taken nor reserved; the value is trimmed of surrounding whitespace before those checks run. A missing, blank, invalid, reserved or taken subdomain returns `409 Conflict` with a `success: false` body rather than a validation error. Note that a successful request locks the subdomain in the shared cache for 60 seconds *before* the account is created, so retrying a request that failed with a `422` returns a `409` until the lock expires.
---@field suite_trial? zendesk.TrialAccountInputSuiteTrial Provisions a `suite` trial SKU instead of the default `support` SKU. Also copied into `trial_extras.suite_trial` when present. Declared as a boolean in the parameter gate, which also accepts and coerces the string and integer spellings `"true"`, `"1"`, `"on"`, `1`, `"false"`, `"0"` and `0`.
---@field utc_offset? zendesk.TrialAccountInputUtcOffset Time zone for the new account, given either as a UTC offset (for example `7` or `"7"`) or as an ActiveSupport time zone name. Resolved by `Account::Localization.utc_to_tz` into `account.time_zone`; an unrecognised, empty or `null` value falls back to `Eastern Time (US & Canada)`.
---@field zendesk_suite_trial? zendesk.TrialAccountInputZendeskSuiteTrial Provisions a Zendesk Suite trial (a professional-plan `zendesk_suite` SKU expiring in 14 days) rather than the default SKU. Enabled by any value the parameter gate coerces to true (`1`, `"1"`, `true`, `"true"`, `"on"`); every other value is ignored. Evaluated before `employee_service_suite_trial`.

---Provisions an Employee Service Suite trial (a professional-plan `employee_service_suite` SKU expiring in 14 days) with `account.account_type` set to `pre_spp`. Enabled by any value the parameter gate coerces to true (`1`, `"1"`, `true`, `"true"`, `"on"`). Takes effect only when `zendesk_suite_trial` is not set, which is evaluated first.
---@alias zendesk.TrialAccountInputEmployeeServiceSuiteTrial boolean|string|number

---Legacy switch for the account's product configuration. PLATOPS-1372 removed the multiproduct branch and the legacy Classic fallback from `create`, so this controller no longer reads the value and it has no effect on which service handles the request. It is still accepted by the parameter gate and forwarded verbatim to the account service like every other permitted property; whether it affects provisioning is decided by the account service, outside this repository. The value the account service returns is echoed back as `account.multiproduct` in the response body.
---@alias zendesk.TrialAccountInputMultiproduct boolean|string|number

---Single sign-on configuration for the new account. Accepted and forwarded to the account service verbatim; this controller does not read it.
---@alias zendesk.TrialAccountInputRemoteAuthentication zendesk.TrialAccountRemoteAuthenticationInput|any

---Provisions a `suite` trial SKU instead of the default `support` SKU. Also copied into `trial_extras.suite_trial` when present. Declared as a boolean in the parameter gate, which also accepts and coerces the string and integer spellings `"true"`, `"1"`, `"on"`, `1`, `"false"`, `"0"` and `0`.
---@alias zendesk.TrialAccountInputSuiteTrial boolean|string|number

---Time zone for the new account, given either as a UTC offset (for example `7` or `"7"`) or as an ActiveSupport time zone name. Resolved by `Account::Localization.utc_to_tz` into `account.time_zone`; an unrecognised, empty or `null` value falls back to `Eastern Time (US & Canada)`.
---@alias zendesk.TrialAccountInputUtcOffset number|string

---Provisions a Zendesk Suite trial (a professional-plan `zendesk_suite` SKU expiring in 14 days) rather than the default SKU. Enabled by any value the parameter gate coerces to true (`1`, `"1"`, `true`, `"true"`, `"on"`); every other value is ignored. Evaluated before `employee_service_suite_trial`.
---@alias zendesk.TrialAccountInputZendeskSuiteTrial boolean|string|number

