---The writable attributes accepted when creating a user field.
---@class zendesk.UserFieldInput
---@field active? boolean|distilled.Null Whether this field is available. Defaults to `true`; sending null has the same effect
---@field custom_field_options? zendesk.UserFieldInputCustomFieldOptionsList|distilled.Null Required for `dropdown`, `tagger`, and `multiselect` fields; at least one option must be supplied. The array order determines each option's position. Do not send this for any other field type. It is not ignored: the options association is defined on every field type, so the options are persisted against a field that can never present them, leaving unreachable rows behind. Sending null is equivalent to omitting the key: no options are created. An empty array behaves the same way on create.
---@field description? string|distilled.Null User-defined description of this field's purpose. Defaults to the field's `title` when omitted; sending null has the same effect and writes the `title` into `description`, rather than leaving it empty.
---@field key string A unique key that identifies this custom field. Used for updating the field and referencing in placeholders. May contain only letters, digits, and underscores, must contain at least one letter or underscore, and is limited to 255 characters. The values `count`, `reorder`, `check_permissions`, and `show_many` are reserved. Cannot be changed after creation.
---@field permissions? zendesk.UserFieldPermissionsInput|distilled.Null
---@field position? number|distilled.Null Ordering of the field relative to other fields. The field is inserted at this index in the account's existing user field order; when omitted or null, the field is appended last.
---@field raw_description? string|distilled.Null The dynamic content placeholder for the description. See [Dynamic Content](/api-reference/ticketing/ticket-management/dynamic_content/). When supplied, this value is written to `description` and any `description` sent alongside it is discarded. Sending null is accepted and discarded: `description` is left as sent.
---@field raw_title? string|distilled.Null The dynamic content placeholder for the title. See [Dynamic Content](/api-reference/ticketing/ticket-management/dynamic_content/). When supplied, this value is written to `title` and any `title` sent alongside it is discarded. Sending null is accepted and discarded: `title` is left as sent.
---@field regexp_for_validation? string For `regexp` fields only. The validation pattern for a field value to be deemed valid
---@field relationship_filter? zendesk.UserFieldInputRelationshipFilter|distilled.Null For `lookup` fields only. A filter definition that limits which records the field's autocomplete returns. Sending null is equivalent to omitting it and leaves the field with no filter.
---@field relationship_target_type? string|distilled.Null Required for `lookup` fields; omitting it returns a 400. A representation of what type of object the field references. For user fields the options are `zen:user`, `zen:organization`, `zen:ticket`, `zen:attachment`, or `zen:custom_object:{key}` where key is a custom object key. Values are downcased by the API. `zen:article`, `zen:group`, and `zen:brand` are not valid on user fields and are rejected. Cannot be changed after creation. Sending null is equivalent to omitting it, so a `lookup` field still returns a 400.
---@field tag? string|distilled.Null For `checkbox` fields only. A tag added to the user when the checkbox field is selected. Supplying `tag` for any other field type fails validation. Values are downcased by the API. Sending null is accepted and leaves the field with no tag.
---@field title string The title of the user field
---@field type? zendesk.UserFieldInputType|string|distilled.Null The type of the user field. Determines which additional attributes are relevant (for example `custom_field_options` is required for `dropdown`, `tagger`, and `multiselect`). Defaults to `text` when not specified. Cannot be changed after creation. Sending null is equivalent to omitting it and creates a `text` field.

