---A single option for a `dropdown` user field, created or updated in place. Fields created with `type: tagger` are
---dropdown fields and are also supported. `multiselect` fields are not: this endpoint returns 404 for them, and their
---options must be managed through the `custom_field_options` array on Update User Field.
---
---Supplying `id` updates that option. When `id` is omitted or null, the API looks up an option on the field with the
---same `value`, whether that option is active or previously deleted. If one is found it is updated in place, restored if
---it had been deleted, and the response is a 200 rather than a 201 — so reusing an existing `value` silently mutates
---that option instead of creating a new one. Otherwise a new option is created.
---@class zendesk.UserFieldOptionCreateOrUpdateInput
---@field id? number|distilled.Null The id of an existing, active option to update. A deleted option's id is not accepted and returns 404; a deleted option can only be restored through the `value` match below. Omit `id` or send null to create a new option, or to match an existing one by `value`.
---@field name string The presentation name of the option
---@field position? number The relative position of the option in the field's option list. Defaults to the end of the list when creating a new option
---@field value? string The tag value applied to the user when the option is selected. Must be unique across the account's field options. Required when creating an option; when updating an existing option by `id`, omitting it leaves the current value unchanged.

---An option for a `dropdown`, `tagger`, or `multiselect` custom user field.
