---@field id zendesk.UserFieldOptionUpdateInputId The id of an existing option to update in place. To add a new option, send null or an empty string. The key itself is mandatory on every entry: an option with no `id` key is rejected with a `BlankValue` error.
---@field name? string The presentation name of the option. Must not be blank. Required when adding a new option
---@field raw_name? string|distilled.Null The dynamic content placeholder for the option's name. See [Dynamic Content](/api-reference/ticketing/ticket-management/dynamic_content/). When supplied, this value is written to `name` and any `name` sent alongside it is discarded. Sending null is accepted and discarded: `name` is left as sent.
---@field value? string The tag value applied to the user when the option is selected. Must be unique across the account's field options. Required when adding a new option; when updating an existing option by `id`, omitting it leaves the current value unchanged. When adding an option whose `value` matches one that was previously deleted, the deleted option is restored instead. That match is case-sensitive, so a value differing only in case does not restore the old option.

