---@class zendesk.UserIdentityResponse
---@field identity? zendesk.UserIdentityObject

---A partial update. Only the properties listed here can be changed on an existing identity - `type` and
---`primary` cannot, and are ignored if sent. Omitting a property leaves it unchanged.
---
---One exception to "leaves it unchanged": if the identity is a non-primary email identity of the account
---owner, sending an `identity` object unverifies the identity and sends a verification email. The
---trigger is the presence of the object - its contents make no difference, and `verified: true` or
---`verification_method: low` does not prevent it. Sending `"identity": null` instead of an object is the
---one way to avoid it, because the whole update branch is then skipped. The account owner's primary
---email identity cannot be updated at all.
---@class zendesk.UserIdentityUpdateInput
---@field auto_ownership? boolean|distilled.Null When true, sets the email identity to "owned", or to "shared" if another user owns the address. See [Shared email](/api-reference/ticketing/users/user_identities/#shared-email).
---@field deliverable_state? zendesk.UserIdentityUpdateInputDeliverableState|string|distilled.Null Clears the undeliverable state of an email identity, so that Zendesk resumes sending to it. `deliverable` is the only value that has any effect, and only on an `email` identity that is currently undeliverable. Every other value, including null, is ignored.
---@field ownership? zendesk.UserIdentityUpdateInputOwnership|string|distilled.Null Sets the email identity to "owned" or "shared". See [Shared email](/api-reference/ticketing/users/user_identities/#shared-email).
---@field value? string|distilled.Null The new identifier for this identity. Changing the value resets `verification_method` to `none`, so the identity becomes unverified unless the same request also sets `verified` or `verification_method`. null is accepted and ignored - the current value is kept. It does not clear the value.
---@field verification_method? zendesk.UserIdentityUpdateInputVerificationMethod|string|distilled.Null Verifies (`low`) or unverifies (`none`) the identity. Only `none` and `low` are accepted here; the higher methods (`sso`, `embed`, `full`) are set by the corresponding authentication flows. Ignored for identities that belong to the account owner. `phone_number` and `agent_forwarding` identities are re-verified on every save, so `none` has no effect on them. null is **not** ignored here: it is treated like `none` and unverifies the identity. Because this property wins over `verified`, sending `verified: true` alongside `verification_method: null` unverifies it.
---@field verified? boolean|distilled.Null Verifies (`true`) or unverifies (`false`) the identity. null is **not** ignored here: it is treated like `false` and unverifies the identity. Equivalent to setting `verification_method` to `low` or `none`. Deprecated - use `verification_method` instead. Ignored when `verification_method` is also sent - that property wins. Ignored for identities that belong to the account owner. `phone_number` and `agent_forwarding` identities are re-verified on every save, so they cannot be unverified through this endpoint.

---Clears the undeliverable state of an email identity, so that Zendesk resumes sending to it. `deliverable` is the only value that has any effect, and only on an `email` identity that is currently undeliverable. Every other value, including null, is ignored.
---@alias zendesk.UserIdentityUpdateInputDeliverableState "deliverable"

---Sets the email identity to "owned" or "shared". See [Shared email](/api-reference/ticketing/users/user_identities/#shared-email).
---@alias zendesk.UserIdentityUpdateInputOwnership "owned"|"shared"

---Verifies (`low`) or unverifies (`none`) the identity. Only `none` and `low` are accepted here; the
---higher methods (`sso`, `embed`, `full`) are set by the corresponding authentication flows.
---
---Ignored for identities that belong to the account owner. `phone_number` and `agent_forwarding`
---identities are re-verified on every save, so `none` has no effect on them.
---
---null is **not** ignored here: it is treated like `none` and unverifies the identity. Because this
---property wins over `verified`, sending `verified: true` alongside `verification_method: null`
---unverifies it.
---@alias zendesk.UserIdentityUpdateInputVerificationMethod "none"|"low"

